  Our trapezoidal differentiator is a ratio:

     2     1 - 1/z       2  -  2/z       2 z  -  2
    --- * ---------  =  -----------  =  -----------
     T     1 + 1/z       T  +  T/z       T z  +  T

  The numerator is:    2 z  -  2
  The denominator is:  T z  +  T

  They're both affine functions of z. Affine functions are linear.
  So a trapezoidal differentiator is a ratio of linear functions of z.

