    Re (ζ)  =  cos (2 ξ)  =  cos² (ξ)  -  sin² (ξ)
    Im (ζ)  =  sin (2 ξ)  =  2 cos (ξ) sin (ξ)

  Then:
 
    - sin² (x/2)  =  cos (x)  -  cos² (x/2)    <=>    sin² (x/2)  =  cos² (x/2)  -  cos (x)    <=>    1  -  cos² (x/2)  =  cos² (x/2)  -  cos (x)

    <=>    1  -  2 cos² (x/2)  =  - cos (x)    <=>    2 cos² (x/2)  =  cos (x)  +  1
                            _________________
                           ⎟  cos (x)  +  1
    <=>    cos (x/2)  =  ± ⎟ ---------------
                           ⎷        2

  and:

    cos² (x/2)  =  cos (x)  +  sin² (x/2)    <=>    1  -  sin² (x/2)  =  cos (x)  +  sin² (x/2)    <=>    2 sin² (x/2)  =  1  -  cos (x)
                            _________________
                           ⎟  1  -  cos (x)
    <=>    sin (x/2)  =  ± ⎟ ---------------
                           ⎷        2

  We know that  tan (x)  is positive when  0 < x < π/2  and:

    ωc T/2  =  π fc / f_s    and    fc  <  Nyquist  =  f_s / 2    so    fc / f_s  <  1 / 2    <=>    π fc / f_s  <  π/2

