              a0 ( 1  -  cos (ωc T) )  +  a1 sin (ωc T)  +  a2 ( 1  +  cos (ωc T) )           //    the unit-cutoff normalisation,
                                                                                              //    so there's a strong probability that several analog coefficients
            b0 ( 1  -  cos (ωc T) )  -  b1 sin (ωc T)  +  b2 ( 1  +  cos (ωc T) )             //    will be equal to 1.
    β2  =  -----------------------------------------------------------------------            //    
